From: mscharged-port
Subject: Keep the disc-message images as host-filled storage
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

The decompilation generates Game/FE/DiscMessageImages.inc from the original
main.dol: the compressed loading and disc-error images that LidOpenMessage.cpp
draws. The port ships no game data, so natively the include keeps each image's
original name and size as writable storage, and the host copies the player's
own images into it before the original entry, after checking the main.dol
hash. charged_disc_message_image hands the host each image in the retail table
order. The sizes are per version; both European revisions have the same images.

diff --git a/include/Game/FE/DiscMessageImages.inc b/include/Game/FE/DiscMessageImages.inc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..31a3591
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/Game/FE/DiscMessageImages.inc
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
